{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/998587-infernals-homebrew-charm-compilation-2e","id":998587,"title":"Infernals Homebrew Charm Compilation [2e]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Infernal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-04T20:23:30-07:00","id":998587,"title":"Infernals Homebrew Charm Compilation [2e]","content":"Hello Everyone,<br /> I've been compiling a PDF compilation of the majority of the homebrew charms, and I would like to share it with you all: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B9fvi4vAlq0nVy0tRlMwV2xWdmc\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B9...y0tRlMwV2xWdmc</a><br /> <br /> EDIT: Here's the ODT (Open Office) file that the PDF is generated from: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B9fvi4vAlq0nTUJqZ0N4alRWYlk\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B9...UJqZ0N4alRWYlk</a><br /> <br /> EDIT2: I have been spammed by bots asking for edit access on those two files, they are there to host you to download the files, not for you to get access rights other than viewing. I manually edit the real document on my desktop and then upload it in the same share slot with the updated info. I use this thread to collate user submissions here, and anything you want added I will add with the least changes to formatting I can in order to make it work in Open Office and/or pdfs. Preservation is the idea, not being editorial. Thanks for everyone so far!<br /> <br /> Please let me know if I've missed anything, and I will add them to the archive. I know I'm missing a lot that got taken down with the old wiki, especially the interesting fan-made Yozi.<br /> <br /> PS: I don't own anything in the posted document, and I compile them only to archive them against bitrot. This document is in the public domain, and is covered by the CC0 license, do with it what you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12120-bitterwalnut","user":"bitterWalnut","date":". 03-30-2025, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12120-bitterwalnut","name":"bitterWalnut","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T05:35:44-08:00","id":1008891,"title":"","content":"Added the Maradukth and Ta\u2019akozoka charms from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/866610-old-infernal-charmsets\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...rnal-charmsets</a><br /> <br /> The link above auto-updates when the PDF gets stuff added to it. I can share the ODT too, if people want that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12120-bitterwalnut","name":"bitterWalnut","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T00:08:50-08:00","id":1010083,"title":"","content":"The Ta'akozoka set is missing the last three Charms from here <a href=\"http://ninjasensei.wikidot.com/yozi:taakozoka#toc50\" target=\"_blank\">http://ninjasensei.wikidot.com/yozi:taakozoka#toc50</a><br /> Her Act of Villainy is missing as well, but I don't know where to find that.<br /> <br /> Ninjasensei also has a Gaian set <a href=\"http://ninjasensei.wikidot.com/gaian-charms\" target=\"_blank\">http://ninjasensei.wikidot.com/gaian-charms</a><br /> Not exactly a Yozi, but might be relevant, although it doesn't describe what &quot;Permanent Communion&quot; is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11845,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11845-dredmor","user":"Dredmor","date":". 11-30-2016, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11845-dredmor","name":"Dredmor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T10:37:58-08:00","id":1010699,"title":"","content":"Hi bitterWalnut, I just wanted to let you know that I wrote the Oramus Charms in your document beginning with What Is and What Should Never Be and ending with Ornamental Lunatic Pyre Shintai. That set of Charms is separate from the other Oramus Charms in your document and work on very different assumptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T16:55:03-08:00","id":1010869,"title":"","content":"Changes:<br /> - We are now at 1088 pages of archives. I wonder how many core books that is?<br /> - Added in all of the following charms I could find:<br /> - Zuratha (just a few, it appears the rest aren't google-able)<br /> - Cyprian (all but the &quot;Resonant Chorus Shintai&quot;, which is missing from the wiki)<br /> - Achsam (I believe this is all of the ones available, updated last in 2015)<br /> - Gaian (missing &quot;Permanent Communion&quot; definition, note added guessing it's like Gaia's version of &quot;Whispers&quot;)<br /> - Fixed the missing and out of date Ta'akozoka charms, still missing her Act of Villainy (thanks Dredmor!)<br /> - Could not find any Hemera charms (sorry!)<br /> <br /> Responses to recent posters (thanks for the feedback, first of all!):<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11845-dredmor\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11845\" data-vbnamecard=\"11845\">Dredmor</a> <br /> - I fixed the Ta'akozoka charms, my wiki mirror was missing them.<br /> - I added the Gaia charms. Can't hurt?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2497\" data-vbnamecard=\"2497\">Brian888</a> <br /> - Thanks for writing the charms, I can only imagine they took a lot of work. When I eventually get around to cleaning up the document, I'll try to group yours together, and mark them correctly. I've been mostly digging these up from half-dead mirror sites, so things have been a little disjointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12120-bitterwalnut","name":"bitterWalnut","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T18:14:31-08:00","id":1012302,"title":"","content":"Sufficient Velocity has tens if not hundreds of custom Infernal Charms in the Exalted thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T15:39:31-08:00","id":1012826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/998587-infernals-homebrew-charm-compilation-2e?p=1012302#post1012302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sufficient Velocity has tens if not hundreds of custom Infernal Charms in the Exalted thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never heard of the site before, but Google turned it up. I'm rather surprised that they have such an extensive Exalted thread over there. Any hints on how to find the good stuff besides &quot;google better&quot;?<br /> <br /> Thanks for the lead, I imagine there's a lot to dig through,<br /> -bitterWalnut<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12120-bitterwalnut","name":"bitterWalnut","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T17:38:19-08:00","id":1012888,"title":"","content":"Added the Theion Expansions from here: <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?663219-Exalted-2-5-Homebrew-28-Theion-Charms\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php...-Theion-Charms</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12120-bitterwalnut","name":"bitterWalnut","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T08:58:49-08:00","id":1013210,"title":"","content":"Added Revlid's Infernal Monster Style Expansions, and added ODT link, just in case you want more interactivity than the PDF can provide. (new ODT link at top, all links auto-update to current version whenever I update it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12120-bitterwalnut","name":"bitterWalnut","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T10:40:18-08:00","id":1013262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bitterWalnut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/998587-infernals-homebrew-charm-compilation-2e?p=1012826#post1012826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've never heard of the site before, but Google turned it up. I'm rather surprised that they have such an extensive Exalted thread over there. Any hints on how to find the good stuff besides &quot;google better&quot;?<br /> <br /> Thanks for the lead, I imagine there's a lot to dig through,<br /> -bitterWalnut</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Use the threadmarks. You'll mostly find demons written by Aleph and EarthScorpion (and me!), but between them there is some stuff like Revlid's Elloge Charms or EarthScorpion's Oramus Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T09:34:08-08:00","id":1018486,"title":"","content":"@ManusDomine: Thanks for the hint, do you think I missed any?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12120-bitterwalnut","name":"bitterWalnut","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T22:49:11-08:00","id":1018703,"title":"","content":"Hi, I wrote Law Breaker's Abrasive Reprisal!<br /> <br /> I never was able to work out mechanically what I wanted out of the charm, but what I wanted was a way for Cecelyne's sand-blaster charms to hunt down law-breakers automatically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11628-dynamesmouse","name":"Dynamesmouse","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T19:03:15-08:00","id":1020753,"title":"","content":"New Revision Up: Found some Hemera charms buried in a wiki mirror, though its just a couple random ones plus a shintai.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12120-bitterwalnut","name":"bitterWalnut","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T18:57:55-07:00","id":1083777,"title":"","content":"New Revision Up: Found an entire new Devil-Tiger,<span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Mandatum Gwyn, </span>from this thread: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/344789-repost-mandatum-gwyn?_=1493170916113\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1493170916113</a><br /> <br /> We are now at just shy of 1130 pages of charms!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12120-bitterwalnut","name":"bitterWalnut","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T05:57:57-07:00","id":1149898,"title":"","content":"New Revision Up: Found two additional homebrew Kimbery charmsets, as well as a the custom charms of the Mirage Of Beauty (which may be a Devil-Tiger). Current page count: 1172, at Revision 369.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12120-bitterwalnut","name":"bitterWalnut","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T15:09:56-07:00","id":1150017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/threads/devil-tiger-baal-shazash.47430/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.rpnation.com/styles/rpnlogo12.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/threads/devil-tiger-baal-shazash.47430/\" target=\"_blank\"> Devil Tiger: Baal-Shazash </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/threads/devil-tiger-baal-shazash.47430/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.rpnation.com/threads/devil-tiger-baal-shazash.47430/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Baal-Shazash The Dragon Astride the World, the Consuming Fire, the Wyrm of Avarice, Draco Tyrannis Draconian Caste Caste Abilities: Bureaucracy, Investigation, Martial Arts, Occult, Presence Anima Banner: Draconian animas typically involve dragon imagery and resemble either fire, or... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Feel free to add my Devil-Tiger. There's several changes I would make to them now, but those are the last published version, and it's not likely they'll ever see play again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T19:46:02-07:00","id":1150051,"title":"","content":"Hot damn, this saves me some trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T16:58:06-07:00","id":1310631,"title":"","content":"New Revision Up: (Revision 371) Added in all of the yozi/infernal material I could find from The Book of Ten Thousand Scorpions (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/pub?id=1jmxwx7FPXA-jzWJiv2fyCGeJQGQu2QomFTs5j45mPec#h.tnuztspha9j7\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/pub...h.tnuztspha9j7</a>) and the two works from Earthscorpion that the Book linked to, Oramus (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19fBSHGZ-jcyjD9VGM56pEw9QQPULRBKJmcgEKpa9dY4/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...gEKpa9dY4/edit</a>) and Szoreny (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wiRjpZVuyCmhaPXC5vyFFBvTLe7umnUzyzrXcBJZ6mI/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...rXcBJZ6mI/edit</a>). All of the content is amazing.<br /> <br /> Compilation Link is always updated in the main OP.<br /> <br /> New link, not actually in the compilation: my personal modified/expanded/merged Metagaos charmset (thanks to Revlid for the base, and whoever wrote up Ta'akazoka and Ikanii; these are the basis for the expanded charms): <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GOysKqKVmXxhT0vvQzpK3qaSX2RZvMvR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GOy...ew?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12120-bitterwalnut","name":"bitterWalnut","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-26T11:57:08-07:00","id":1495629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bitterWalnut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/998587-infernals-homebrew-charm-compilation-2e?p=1010869#post1010869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changes:<br /> - Gaian (missing \u201cPermanent Communion\u201d definition, note added guessing it's like Gaia's version of \u201cWhispers\u201d)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gaian Charms are from Servants of Gaia which does include a Gaian version of Whispers but Communion is actually her equivalent of Clarity. General setting and rules concept in part one, charms in part two, the appendix never actually got done. <br /> Servants of Gaia WiP part 1: <a href=\"http://keychain.patternspider.net/other/gaia1to3wip.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://keychain.patternspider.net/other/gaia1to3wip.pdf</a><br /> <br /> Servants of Gaia WiP part 2: <a href=\"http://keychain.patternspider.net/other/gaia4wip.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://keychain.patternspider.net/other/gaia4wip.pdf</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27633-the-froggy-ninja","name":"The Froggy Ninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-30T07:18:40-07:00","id":1549642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Froggy Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/998587-infernals-homebrew-charm-compilation-2e?p=1495629#post1495629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gaian Charms are from Servants of Gaia which does include a Gaian version of Whispers but Communion is actually her equivalent of Clarity. General setting and rules concept in part one, charms in part two, the appendix never actually got done.<br /> Servants of Gaia WiP part 1: <a href=\"http://keychain.patternspider.net/other/gaia1to3wip.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://keychain.patternspider.net/other/gaia1to3wip.pdf</a><br /> <br /> Servants of Gaia WiP part 2: <a href=\"http://keychain.patternspider.net/other/gaia4wip.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://keychain.patternspider.net/other/gaia4wip.pdf</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it looks like you have those charms nicely uploaded and formatted already, I will leave that to you, since my technique is literally just copy/paste. For anyone who has their own docs like that, I highly suggest posting them to a handful of places, just in case there is yet another hosting site going down for no adequately explained reason (looking at you Wikia).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12120-bitterwalnut","name":"bitterWalnut","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}